      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Additional idea: give us a SDK3 parameter that is true when the menu is open. That way it's up to us to display some kind of effect when that happens.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-09-07T09:52:39.749Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "All the menus in the game are only visible locally. The reason of this choice is obvious, it's only your business what you're doing inside them. But what if other users could see an empty menu screen where your actual menu is?\nI think it may help with immersion to be able to know at first glance if someone is busy in their menu instead of seeing them moving their hands touching something that doesn't exist.\nFor privacy/preference reasons (maybe not everyone wants that to show) it should be toggleable in the settings (for both showing it to others and seeing it from others).\nPS: got this idea from Borderlands 2, where you can see a hologram in front of players when they're using the menu. It's kinda neat.",
